{title: 222 - Hark! Ten Thousand Harps and Voices}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #222 • HARWELL • 8.7.9.7.7.8.6.5}
{lyricist: Thomas Kelly}
{composer: Lowell Mason}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 222}
{meta: tune HARWELL}
{meta: meter 8.7.9.7.7.8.6.5}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Hark! ten thousand harps [C]and voices
[F/A]Sound the [C7]note of praise above;
[F]Jesus reigns, and heaven [C]rejoices,
[F/A]Jesus [C7]reigns, the God of love:
[C7]See, He sits on [F]yonder throne;
[F]Jesus rules the world alone.
[C]Alleluia! Alleluia!
[F]Alleluia! [C7]Amen.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]King of glory, reign [C]forever,
[F/A]Thine an [C7]everlasting [F]crown;
[F]Nothing from Thy love [C]shall sever
[F/A]Those [C7]whom Thou hast made Thine own;
[C7]Happy objects [F]of Thy grace,
[F]Destined to behold Thy face.
[C]Alleluia! Alleluia!
[F]Alleluia! [C7]Amen.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Savior, hasten Thine [C]appearing;
[F/A]Bring, O [C7]bring the glorious [F]day,
[F]When, the awful summons [C]hearing,
[F/A]Heaven [C7]and [F]earth [C7]shall pass away:;
[C7]Then, with golden [F]harps we'll sing,
[F]"Glory, glory to our King!"
[C]Alleluia! Alleluia!
[F]Alleluia! [C7]Amen.
{end_of_verse}
